From: Paul Zhang <paul@studio-vaai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mf2-catalog: find decomposing code points from a table

The writer's canonical-equivalence map (`writer::nfc_map::build`) looked
for every code point whose decomposition stays inside a catalog's keys by
decomposing all 1,114,112 of them: 5-6 ms per catalog with a variable or a
variant key, and about 8 ms in WebAssembly, where the SDK compiles a host's
override at run time.

Only the 2,081 code points whose canonical decomposition is not themselves
(Hangul syllables aside) can qualify, besides the keys' own characters, so
the builder now visits those, listed as 241 ranges in
`writer/decomposing.rs`. The map comes out the same; a compile with a
variable takes about 20 µs. A test rebuilds the list from
`unicode-normalization` and prints the current one when it is out of date.

Upstream: not proposed (rust-mf2 d598787)
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
